 A default method is used inside an interface.
 👉 Normally, interfaces only had method declarations (no body).
 But starting from Java 8, you can add methods with implementation using default.

 Example:
interface MyInterface {
    default void show() {
        System.out.println("This is a default method");
    }
}
Why it exists:
To add new methods to interfaces without breaking existing classes
Helps with backward compatibility.

